    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3j2mqey",
      "content": "1. Madhya Pradesh was formed on which date?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m8eqmfr",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) 15 August 1947",
        "B) 26 January 1950",
        "C) 1 November 1956",
        "D) 1 November 2000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2dn83wr",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - 1 November 1956 (MP Foundation Day)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rhm7m0x",
      "content": "2. The Bhimbetka Rock Shelters were discovered by:"
    },
    {
      "id": "2zajdyv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) D.R. Bhandarkar",
        "B) V.S. Wakankar",
        "C) John Marshall",
        "D) Alexander Cunningham"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pjw7pq1",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - V.S. Wakankar (in 1957-58)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g15yf8z",
      "content": "3. Sanchi Stupa was originally built by:"
    },
    {
      "id": "ocglmqa",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Harsha",
        "B) Chandragupta Maurya",
        "C) Emperor Ashoka",
        "D) Samudragupta"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "a7fueze",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Emperor Ashoka</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5taeheu",
      "content": "4. The famous Tansen, one of the Navratnas of Akbar, was born in:"
    },
    {
      "id": "kpgtgk5",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Agra",
        "B) Gwalior",
        "C) Ujjain",
        "D) Bhopal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qgh29gy",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Gwalior</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5phmdjc",
      "content": "5. Raja Bhoj, who built the Bhojtal (Upper Lake) at Bhopal, belonged to which dynasty?"
    },
    {
      "id": "w9h490v",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Chandela",
        "B) Gond",
        "C) Paramara",
        "D) Tomar"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "oxuii8p",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Paramara dynasty</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "ln0ev3q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.2 Multiple Choice Questions – Geography"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pnsto3x",
      "content": "6. The highest peak of Madhya Pradesh is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 12: PRACTICE QUESTIONS – MADHYA PRADESH GK",
      "id": "vqwttqb"
    },
    {
      "id": "0lcu1ut",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Amarkantak",
        "B) Dhupgarh",
        "C) Janapav",
        "D) Tamia"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vqv6tpv",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Dhupgarh (1350m), Pachmarhi</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "talmzcz",
      "content": "7. The Narmada River originates from:"
    },
    {
      "id": "2yxjqf7",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Pachmarhi",
        "B) Betul",
        "C) Amarkantak",
        "D) Janapav"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oq1ao9n",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Amarkantak (Anuppur district)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "prr1qbg",
      "content": "8. Madhya Pradesh is called the 'Tiger State of India' because it has:"
    },
    {
      "id": "6j3iahv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Largest tiger reserve area",
        "B) Highest number of tigers",
        "C) First tiger reserve in India",
        "D) First White Tiger"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rvzq8li",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Highest number of tigers in India</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8aozdh7",
      "content": "9. Malanjkhand in Balaghat district is famous for:"
    },
    {
      "id": "adhmvqv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Diamond mining",
        "B) Gold mining",
        "C) Copper mining",
        "D) Coal mining"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7lx2ncj",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Copper mining (Largest copper mine in Asia)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3l193dt",
      "content": "10. The Chambal Wildlife Sanctuary is primarily known for protection of:"
    },
    {
      "id": "c1narqe",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Bengal Tiger",
        "B) Barasingha",
        "C) Indian Gharial",
        "D) Asiatic Lion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f4fl8s9",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Indian Gharial (also river dolphin and crocodile)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "3sldw4a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.3 Multiple Choice Questions – Culture and Miscellaneous"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m6ygfyd",
      "content": "11. The Bhagoria Haat festival is associated with which tribe?"
    },
    {
      "id": "vb3p6rq",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Gond",
        "B) Bhil and Bhilala",
        "C) Baiga",
        "D) Korku"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aajf2in",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Bhil and Bhilala (Jhabua, Alirajpur)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6tixvtl",
      "content": "12. Maheshwari Sarees are woven in:"
    },
    {
      "id": "ivcbevm",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Chanderi, Ashoknagar",
        "B) Maheshwar, Khargone",
        "C) Bagh, Dhar",
        "D) Ujjain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hep5mgo",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Maheshwar, Khargone district</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6exapn7",
      "content": "13. The first white tiger in modern history was discovered in which district of MP?"
